 "title": "Basketball: dribble to the frontcourt",
 "category": "basketball-and-rackets",
 "time_limit_s": 60.0,
 "stages": [
  "dribble",
  "past the free-throw line",
  "in the frontcourt"
 ],
 "rulebook": "FIBA Official Basketball Rules 2024: Art. 2 (court), Art. 3 and the Basketball Equipment appendix (size-7 ball), Art. 13 (how the ball is played), Art. 14 (control: a player holds a live ball), Art. 23 (out of bounds), Art. 24 (dribbling), Art. 25 (travelling), Art. 28.1.3 (when a dribbled ball is in the frontcourt)",
 "deviations": [
  "the player's hands: the H1-2's own Inspire five-finger hands (six drives each: four fingers, the thumb's flexion and rotation; fingertip forces 20 N, the thumb 30 N), each closed by one command; the ball is held in the two hands by contact and friction alone (nothing is welded) and can slip or drop; it has left your hands when no hand has been on it for 0.03 s. The fingers' rubber pads absorb the ball (critically damped), so a dribbling hand gives the ball its speed by its own motion; the floor keeps the ball's rule-book rebound.",
  "Art. 24.1.3 (carrying the ball, a hand under it): judged by where a hand touches the ball: a touch from below (the hand's lowest contact point on the ball lower than the ball's centre by more than 0.3 of its radius) that lasts longer than 0.1 s carries the ball; a hand on top of it or on its side pushes it.",
  "Art. 24.1.2 (the ball 'comes to rest' in a hand) is read as: a hand's touch of the ball that lasts longer than 0.3 s. A dribble that has ended cannot legally be started again (Art. 24.2), so a ball that comes to rest in a hand, or is touched by both hands at once, ends the attempt.",
  "Art. 13: every touch of the ball by a part of you other than a hand is a violation, also while the ball is held at the start (no ball held against the chest or between the forearms); intent (an accidental touch of a leg is legal in the rule book) cannot be judged.",
  "Art. 14 / 24 give no distance for 'control' of a dribbled ball: here the ball's centre must stay within 2.0 m (horizontally) of your pelvis, so that a ball thrown ahead and walked after is not a dribble.",
  "Art. 28 (eight seconds to reach the frontcourt) is not applied: the attempt lasts at most 60 s of robot time."
 ],
 "texts": {
  "sentence": "Dribble the basketball, which starts held in your two hands, from the end line across the centre line, 14 m up the court, one hand at a time, without a dribbling, carrying or travelling violation.",
  "rules": "A FIBA court, 28.0 m by 15.0 m inside its boundary lines (lines 0.05 m wide); the centre line's axis is 14.0 m from the end line. The ball is a size-7 basketball (0.239 m across, 0.62 kg, it keeps 0.85 of its speed in a bounce on the floor). Your hands are five-finger hands, each closed by its grip value (0 open, 1 closed); they hold the ball only by contact and friction: it starts resting on your upturned right hand, the fingers curled a little round it, your left hand on its side, and it can slip or drop. A hand is the palm, the fingers, the thumb and the wrist; a hand is on the ball while it touches the ball, gaps shorter than 0.03 s included; the ball is in your hands while at least one hand is on it, and it has left them once no hand has been on it for 0.03 s. You stand still. Starting the dribble: the first foot you lift makes the other your pivot foot; the pivot foot, and before a foot is lifted either foot, may not slide more than 0.2 m along the floor, and the pivot foot may not leave the floor before the ball has left your hands (a foot has left the floor when it has not touched it for 0.03 s). While the ball is in your hands it may touch no part of you but your hands, and it may not touch the floor. The ball leaving your hands (pushed, dropped or slipped) is the first touch of your dribble. The dribble: after that you play the ball with one hand at a time, by touches that push it to the floor (thrown, tapped, rolled or bounced): between two touches by your hands the ball must have touched the floor; contacts of a hand less than 0.03 s apart are one touch. There is no limit to your steps while the ball is not in a hand. You succeed at the first moment the ball touches the floor in the frontcourt (beyond the centre line's far edge, 14.0 m plus half a line width from the end line) with both your feet in the frontcourt (every point where each foot last touched the floor is beyond that edge), after at least one touch of your dribble after the ball left your hands. You fail if you travel at the start; if the ball touches the floor or a part of you other than a hand while it is in your hands; if, after it has left your hands, a hand's touch lasts longer than 0.3 s (the ball has come to rest in the hand); if a hand carries the ball (it touches the ball from below, its lowest contact point on the ball lower than the ball's centre by more than 0.3 of the ball's radius, for longer than 0.1 s); if both hands touch the ball at the same time; if a hand touches the ball twice without the ball having touched the floor in between; if the ball touches any part of you other than a hand; if the ball's centre is ever more than 2.0 m (horizontally) from your pelvis after it left your hands; if the ball or any part of you touches the floor on or outside a boundary line (out of bounds); if you fall (a fall: your pelvis lower than 0.35 m above the floor, or any part of you other than your feet on the floor); or after 60 s.",
  "venue": "You stand in the backcourt just inside the end line, facing up the court (+x): the end line's inner edge is 0.5 m behind your pelvis and the centre line 14.0 m beyond that edge. The basket of this end is to your right: the court's long axis, with the backboard (its lower edge 2.9 m high, 1.2 m in from the end line) and the ring, is 2.5 m to your right; the side lines are 15.0 m apart, the nearer one 5 m to your left. Painted on the floor: the boundary lines, the restricted area, the free-throw line (5.8 m from the end line) and circle, the three-point line, the centre line and circle. The ball rests on your upturned right hand in front of your chest, its centre about 1.1 m above the floor, 0.39 m ahead of your pelvis and 0.06 m to its right; the right hand's fingers point forwards under it, curled a little round it (grip value 0.3), the left hand's palm is on its left side, open (grip value 0); the start command keeps that hold. A grip value is that hand's closure command: 0 opens the fingers, 1 closes every finger and the thumb until they meet something.",
  "difficulty": "The ball keeps 85 % of its speed in a bounce but a hand absorbs it, so every touch has to push it down and forward again by the hand's own motion to where the hand will be, with a hand about 8 cm wide and a ball 24 cm across, for 14 m, on a body whose walking gait covers about 0.7 m/s, drifts in heading, and is disturbed by every push of the arm. The built-in walking gait steps on the spot even at a zero command, so the ball has to leave the hands before it starts."
 },
